FILES
~~~~~
Eclipse.library		- V35.24	- This goes into your libs: dir


Userinfo		- V2.02b	- Gives you extra info about a user.
					  Can be used as a function for the
					  users.  If so, use an entry like
					  this in your Menus.BBS file:

   1 CON -- "UserInfo «GETSTACK»«Name (or part name) of user to view? »"

					  UserInfo works by having the name
					  or part name entered after the
					  program name.


Owner			- V2.02		- Provides information about a file
					  in one of the file areas.  Mainly
					  for use by the users.  You need a
					  entry into your Menu.BBS file eg.

           O CON M  "Owner «FILEPATH»«GETSTACK»«File to view? »"

					  Extra information can be provided
					  to the user via the use of an text
					  file that you can make in the same
					  directory as your file.  It is
					  optional to have an entry.  This
					  way you can provide extra info for
					  just certain files.  This file is
					  called FilesInfo.BBS.  Entries
					  should be set out as below:

Filename				<--- Name of file
the linesfollowing the name of the file are typed below the option.  You can
have as many lines as you like.
---					<--- Use these 3 minus signs to
					     signify the end of end of the
					     description


Logtag			- V2.01		  Adds an entry into the Log.bbs
					  text file.  This allows you to
					  find out in more detail what your
					  users have been doing on the
					  system.  Simply place the wanted
					  string after the name (and it will
					  be entered into the log (with the
					  date and time as well))


UserPurge		- V1.11		  Cleans up the User.BBS file.
					  Removes "In-Active" users, and
					  users that have been deleted.  The
					  number of days that is the cut-off
					  marker is variable, but the
					  defualt is 30 days.


NewUser			- V1.02		  Allows you to quickly find out all
					  of the new users that have logged
					  onto your system.  It will look
					  for users that have an access level
					  of DISGRACE (normal NewUser level)
					  and then ask you if you want to
					  validate them.  Validating them
					  will increase their access up to
					  NORMAL level, and set their times
					  and download limits accordingly.
					  As of version 1.01, you also have
					  the option to Delete a user instead
					  of validating them.  This will just
					  mark the user as Dead, and then,
					  the next time you run UserPurge,
					  they will be removed from the User-
					  Base.  No arguments are required,
					  just run it in the same directory
					  as your Falcon.cfg file.


TypeBack		- V1.02		  Types a ASCII text file line by
					  line, backwards.  It reads the
					  whole file, then starting with the
					  last line, it works it's way to the
					  top of the file.  You can interrupt
					  the output at anytime, simply by
					  hitting CTRL-C.


Access			- V1.01		  Permits you to limit access by your
					  users to external programs.  Can
					  either be included into a ARexx
					  program, or used as part of a
					  normal script.  Access will return
					  either NO return code (0) if the
					  user is allows access; or it will
					  return WARN (5), if not permitted
					  access to the function.

					  Access makes use of two extra
					  text files.  These are:

		Accessx.dat		  This file has the names of the users
					  that have access to the function.
					  Each name should be on a seperate
					  line, with a single CR seperating
					  each entry.

		Accessx.deny		  This is a text file that will be
					  typed if the user is not allowed
					  access.  Change it to whatever you
					  want it to say.

					  The "x"'s in the above two text
					  files names relate to special 
					  identifiers that allows you to
					  have many different programs using
					  access to limit access.
					  


USAGE
~~~~~
	UserInfo	<Username/Partname>
	LogTag		<String to go into Logfile>
	UserPurge	<number of days>
	Owner		<Path/Filename to examine>
	NewUser
	TypeBack	<Path/filename>
	Access		<Num><Username>
